# Accepted findings. Each entry states why, and how to re-check it.
#
# GO-2026-5932 / golang.org/x/crypto
#   The advisory is that golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe
#   by design. It has no fix because the whole module version range is flagged,
#   and trivy matches on module version rather than on reachability.
#
#   We import golang.org/x/crypto/argon2 for password hashing. openpgp is not in
#   the build at all. Verify with:
#       go list -deps ./... | grep -i openpgp      # expect no output
#       just vuln                                   # govulncheck: not called
#
#   Remove this entry if openpgp ever enters the dependency graph.
GO-2026-5932
CVE-2026-5932

# CVE-2026-41589 / github.com/charmbracelet/wish
#   SCP path traversal in wish/scp: a client can read or write arbitrary paths
#   through the SCP middleware. There is no fixed version (v1.4.7 is latest),
#   and trivy matches on module version rather than on which packages are built.
#
#   We never register the SCP middleware. Only wish and wish/bubbletea are in
#   the build, for PTY setup and renderer wiring in internal/sshd/session.go.
#   Verify with:
#       go list -deps ./... | grep wish/scp      # expect no output
#       just vuln                                 # govulncheck: not called
#
#   Remove this entry when wish ships a fix, or if wish/scp ever enters the
#   dependency graph.
CVE-2026-41589
